---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Ui.astro';
---

<Base title="Typography">
  <h1>Typography &amp; prose</h1>
  <p>
    Three faces, each with one job — Rye for the masthead, Special Elite
    for department headings and the typewriter utility voice, and Sorts
    Mill Goudy for prose. Everything ships at weight 400: loudness is
    dialled with face, size and tracking, never bold. <code>.mk-prose</code>
    sets the long-form column.
  </p>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>THE THREE FACES</h2>
    <p>Each face has one job; none may do another&rsquo;s.</p>

    <div class="specimen">
      <div class="specimen__row">
        <span class="specimen__label">Rye · masthead &amp; names</span>
        <h1 style="margin: 0;">Taylor&rsquo;s Follies</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="specimen__row">
        <span class="specimen__label">Special Elite · departments</span>
        <h2 style="margin: 0;">THE EVENING PROGRAMME</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="specimen__row">
        <span class="specimen__label">Special Elite · subhead</span>
        <h3 style="margin: 0;">NOTES FROM THE WINGS</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="specimen__row">
        <span class="specimen__label">Special Elite · utility</span>
        <span class="mk-kicker" style="margin: 0;">DETROIT · TUESDAY EVENING · ONE NIGHT ONLY</span>
      </div>
      <div class="specimen__row">
        <span class="specimen__label">Goudy · prose</span>
        <p style="margin: 0;">
          Mr. Taylor will attempt the soldering iron a second time; the
          management has moved the front row back six feet.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="specimen__row">
        <span class="specimen__label">Goudy italic · taglines</span>
        <p style="margin: 0; font-style: italic; color: var(--mk-color-text-secondary);">
          &ldquo;More power&rdquo; — the motto of the house
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <pre><code>&lt;h1&gt;Taylor&rsquo;s Follies&lt;/h1&gt;          &lt;!-- Rye — never body, never a button --&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;THE EVENING PROGRAMME&lt;/h2&gt;   &lt;!-- typewriter at display size — caps written in the markup --&gt;
&lt;span class="mk-kicker"&gt;ONE NIGHT ONLY&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Goudy prose for everything spoken.&lt;/p&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>THE LOUDNESS DIAL</h2>
    <p>
      The typewriter face has no bold; tracking is its loudness dial.
      Point-one em is a dateline; point-four em is a proscenium announcement.
      Pick the token for what the line means, not for taste.
    </p>

    <div class="ladder">
      <div class="ladder__row">
        <span class="specimen__label">--mk-track-dept · .08em</span>
        <span class="ladder__sample" style="letter-spacing: var(--mk-track-dept);">A DEPARTMENT SLUG</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ladder__row">
        <span class="specimen__label">--mk-track-mono · .1em</span>
        <span class="ladder__sample" style="letter-spacing: var(--mk-track-mono);">DETROIT · TUESDAY</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ladder__row">
        <span class="specimen__label">--mk-track-nav-sm · .12em</span>
        <span class="ladder__sample" style="letter-spacing: var(--mk-track-nav-sm);">SMALL NAVIGATION</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ladder__row">
        <span class="specimen__label">--mk-track-back · .18em</span>
        <span class="ladder__sample" style="letter-spacing: var(--mk-track-back);">&larr; BACK TO THE LOBBY</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ladder__row">
        <span class="specimen__label">--mk-track-nav · .22em</span>
        <span class="ladder__sample" style="letter-spacing: var(--mk-track-nav);">THE MAIN NAV</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ladder__row">
        <span class="specimen__label">--mk-track-bill-no · .3em</span>
        <span class="ladder__sample" style="letter-spacing: var(--mk-track-bill-no);">BILL NO. 4</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ladder__row">
        <span class="specimen__label">--mk-track-bulletin · .32em</span>
        <span class="ladder__sample" style="letter-spacing: var(--mk-track-bulletin);">BULLETIN</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ladder__row">
        <span class="specimen__label">--mk-track-kicker · .4em</span>
        <span class="ladder__sample" style="letter-spacing: var(--mk-track-kicker);">TONIGHT</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <pre><code>&lt;span style="font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
             letter-spacing: var(--mk-track-kicker);"&gt;TONIGHT&lt;/span&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <section class="mk-card">
    <h2>PROSE</h2>
    <p>
      Wrap long-form matter in <code>.mk-prose</code> — Goudy at a 70ch
      measure, the column a compositor would set. Lists, typewriter code, the
      ruled pull-quote and the miniature struck key (<code>kbd</code>) are all
      in the case.
    </p>

    <div class="mk-prose">
      <p>
        <strong>Tool Time</strong>, presented nightly by the Binford Tool
        Company, stars Mr. Tim Taylor and his assistant Mr. Al Borland. The
        first act is a demonstration; the second act is an apology.
      </p>

      <h3>THE RUNNING ORDER</h3>
      <p>The bill proceeds in a fixed order of acts:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Act I — the demonstration, as rehearsed</li>
        <li>Act II — the improvement, unrehearsed</li>
        <li>
          Act III — the repair
          <ul>
            <li>Mr. Borland stands by with the extinguisher</li>
          </ul>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h3>SETTING THE BILL BY WIRE</h3>
      <p>
        The box office amends an act with <code>PATCH /acts/:id</code>; the
        reply confirms what is now printed:
      </p>
      <pre><code>PATCH /acts/2
&#123; "state": "on the bill", "billing": "second" &#125;
=&gt; 200 &#123; "id": 2, "state": "on the bill" &#125;</code></pre>

      <blockquote>
        <p>
          It is not the applause a man keeps, Tim — it is the neighbours he
          borrows it from.
        </p>
      </blockquote>

      <p>
        Prefer the keys? Press <kbd>G</kbd> to raise the grand drape, or
        <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>B</kbd> for the blackout.
      </p>

      <small>Programme subject to change without notice.</small>
    </div>

    <pre><code>&lt;article class="mk-prose"&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Goudy prose with &lt;code&gt;inline type&lt;/code&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
  &lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;p&gt;The ruled pull quote.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
  &lt;p&gt;Press &lt;kbd&gt;G&lt;/kbd&gt; for the drape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/article&gt;</code></pre>
  </section>

  <style>
    .specimen,
    .ladder {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: var(--mk-space-md);
    }

    .specimen__row,
    .ladder__row {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      align-items: baseline;
      gap: var(--mk-space-xxs) var(--mk-space-lg);
    }

    .specimen__label {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      min-width: 13rem;
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: var(--mk-size-mono-xs);
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      color: var(--mk-color-text-muted);
    }

    .ladder__sample {
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: var(--mk-size-mono);
      color: var(--mk-color-heading);
    }

    section.mk-card + section.mk-card {
      margin-top: var(--mk-space-2xl);
    }

    pre {
      margin-top: var(--mk-space-md);
      padding: 12px 14px;
      background: var(--mk-color-plate);
      border: var(--mk-rule-hair);
      border-left: var(--mk-rule-thick);
      color: var(--mk-color-heading);
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: var(--mk-size-mono-sm);
      line-height: 1.6;
      overflow-x: auto;
    }

    code {
      font-family: var(--mk-font-typewriter);
      font-size: 0.86em;
      background: var(--mk-color-plate);
      border: var(--mk-rule-hair);
      color: var(--mk-color-heading);
      padding: 1px 5px 0;
    }

    pre code {
      background: none;
      border: 0;
      padding: 0;
      font-size: inherit;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
